-- Tests for bc-interpretation-replacement.l4 (Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238, ss 34, 36(1)(b), 36(1)(c), 37).
-- Each expected value was decided from the text before the file was first run. Every limb of a rule is tested on both
-- sides. A case the text does not answer is asserted as the named refusal with its message (NOTES.md, finding 2).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-replacement`


§ `s 34 Amending enactment`
-- 34: "An amending enactment must be construed as part of the enactment that it amends."
#ASSERT `s 34 the enactment is construed as part of the enactment that it amends` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 34 the enactment is construed as part of the enactment that it amends` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 34 speaks only of an amending enactment"

§ `s 36(1)(b) Proceedings commenced under the former enactment`
-- 36 (1)(b): "every proceeding commenced under the former enactment must be continued under and in conformity with the new enactment so far as it may be done consistently with the new enactment"
#ASSERT `s 36(1)(b) the proceeding must be continued under and in conformity with the new enactment` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 36(1)(b) the proceeding must be continued under and in conformity with the new enactment` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 36(1)(b) the proceeding must be continued under and in conformity with the new enactment` TRUE FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 36(1)(b) speaks only of a proceeding commenced under the former enactment"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 36(1)(b) the proceeding must be continued under and in conformity with the new enactment` FALSE TRUE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 36(1) applies only where another enactment is substituted for the repealed one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 36(1)(b) the proceeding must be continued under and in conformity with the new enactment` FALSE FALSE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 36(1) applies only where another enactment is substituted for the repealed one"

§ `s 36(1)(c) Procedure of the new enactment`
-- 36 (1)(c): "the procedure established by the new enactment must be followed as far as it can be adapted in the recovery or enforcement of penalties and forfeitures incurred under the former enactment, in the enforcement of rights existing or accruing under the former enactment, and in a proceeding relating to matters that happened before the repeal"
#ASSERT `s 36(1)(c) the procedure established by the new enactment must be followed` `The recovery or enforcement of penalties and forfeitures incurred under the former enactment` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 36(1)(c) the procedure established by the new enactment must be followed` `The recovery or enforcement of penalties and forfeitures incurred under the former enactment` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 36(1)(c) the procedure established by the new enactment must be followed` `The enforcement of rights existing or accruing under the former enactment` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 36(1)(c) the procedure established by the new enactment must be followed` `The enforcement of rights existing or accruing under the former enactment` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 36(1)(c) the procedure established by the new enactment must be followed` `A proceeding relating to matters that happened before the repeal` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 36(1)(c) the procedure established by the new enactment must be followed` `A proceeding relating to matters that happened before the repeal` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 36(1)(c) the procedure established by the new enactment must be followed` `Something else` TRUE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 36(1)(c) names three situations in which the procedure of the new enactment is followed and no others"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 36(1)(c) the procedure established by the new enactment must be followed` `A proceeding relating to matters that happened before the repeal` FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 36(1) applies only where another enactment is substituted for the repealed one"

§ `s 37 No implications from repeal, amendment, etc.`
-- 37 (1): a repeal, a repeal and substitution, or an amendment "must not be construed to be or to involve either a declaration that the enactment was ... previously in force, or a declaration about the previous state of the law."
-- 37 (2): an amendment "must not be construed to be or to involve a declaration that the law under the enactment prior to the amendment was ... different from the law under the enactment as amended."
-- 37 (3): "An amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision of an enactment must not be construed to be or to involve an adoption of the construction that has by judicial decision or otherwise been placed on the language used in the enactment or on similar language."
-- All 30 cells of the grid (6 things done by 5 things read in): 11 are named by the text and give FALSE; the other 19 are not named and give a refusal.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Repeal of all or part of it` `A declaration that the enactment was, or was considered by those who enacted it to have been, previously in force`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Repeal of all or part of it` `A declaration about the previous state of the law`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Repeal of all or part of it` `A declaration that the law under the enactment before the amendment was, or was considered by those who enacted it to have been, different from the law as amended`
        BECAUSE "s 37 says what must not be read into a repeal, amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision and does not say what may"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Repeal of all or part of it` `An adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise`
        BECAUSE "s 37 says what must not be read into a repeal, amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision and does not say what may"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Repeal of all or part of it` `Something else`
        BECAUSE "s 37 says what must not be read into a repeal, amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision and does not say what may"
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Repeal of it and substitution of another enactment for it` `A declaration that the enactment was, or was considered by those who enacted it to have been, previously in force`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Repeal of it and substitution of another enactment for it` `A declaration about the previous state of the law`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Repeal of it and substitution of another enactment for it` `A declaration that the law under the enactment before the amendment was, or was considered by those who enacted it to have been, different from the law as amended`
        BECAUSE "s 37 says what must not be read into a repeal, amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision and does not say what may"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Repeal of it and substitution of another enactment for it` `An adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise`
        BECAUSE "s 37 says what must not be read into a repeal, amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision and does not say what may"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Repeal of it and substitution of another enactment for it` `Something else`
        BECAUSE "s 37 says what must not be read into a repeal, amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision and does not say what may"
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Amendment of it` `A declaration that the enactment was, or was considered by those who enacted it to have been, previously in force`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Amendment of it` `A declaration about the previous state of the law`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Amendment of it` `A declaration that the law under the enactment before the amendment was, or was considered by those who enacted it to have been, different from the law as amended`)
